      "notes": "All nine zero limits now refuse inspect/read/write before callbacks, provider reads or staging. Prior actual short-read, Windows locked-byte write, exact-name collision, cancellation and target/source preservation proofs remain. Disk-full/flush/close faults and other platforms remain broader obligations; a write lock does not qualify them. Legacy TIFF encoding/publication now preserves a pre-existing fixed-suffix file, checked by a real failing regression before repair. Memory encoding removes the predictable sibling and disk readback; shared byte publication uses the existing exclusive atomic helper. This does not qualify disk-full/flush/close or POSIX ownership faults. The shared panel now revalidates held input identity after a read worker is ready and before publication. An actual changed-file regression fails against the prior installed product and passes after repair. This does not qualify remaining disk-full/flush/close or POSIX faults.",
